# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Build output
/target/

# `docs/reference/` IS committed, deliberately (ADR-0018): docs/ACCEPTANCE.md section 4.5
# requires that the committed docs match what the registries produce, and the diff of a generated
# page is how a change to the public contract becomes reviewable. It is generated by
# `cargo xtask docs` and never hand-edited (AGENTS.md section 2).

# Packages written by scripts/package.sh (ADR-0121)
/dist/

# The coverage-guided fuzzing tier writes its own corpus, its crash artifacts and its build
# output under `fuzz/coverage-guided/`. v0.4.1 §41.4 asks for the corpus to be committed *or*
# stored as a durable CI artifact, and the scheduled workflow caches it between runs; a corpus
# libFuzzer grew to nine hundred files in twenty seconds is not a thing to keep in git. A crash
# *reproducer* is different: it is minimized by hand and committed under `fuzz/artifacts/`,
# where the gate replays it on every run (ADR-0521).
fuzz/coverage-guided/corpus/
fuzz/coverage-guided/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage-guided/target/
